gomad: regenerate adapter anchors for a new module version behind an approval digest
gomadtool adapter-regenerate re-applies an adapter's rewrites by their
exact-occurrence anchors to a candidate module version, prints the changed
upstream source, the proposed anchors, and stale pack bindings, and applies
only with the review's approval digest. The apply stages the adapter
constants, version descriptor, fixture modules, and generated outputs in a
scratch copy, verifies them, and publishes under a lock through a committed
journal that the next run completes.

Adapters are now declared as rewrittenModule specs (gRPC and x/net included,
with base-file rewrites), and prepared source-set pins are computed from
source for every platform, reproducing all 30 checked-in pins on any host.

